      "line_id": "pigeon-line",
      "input_line": "I've just finished the part in Alice where the Pigeon calls her a serpent and she tries to say she's a little girl. That landed close to home: I still stumble over calling myself a manager. Could you quote the sentence where she calls herself a little girl, including how the narrator describes her saying it, and help me think about why naming a new role feels so awkward? Please stay with what I've read.",
